  "body": "## Why this change is needed\n\nA platform reload refreshes the Dart preferences cache, but the pinned Android plugin reads Android's own in-memory preferences. A failed synchronous commit can leave that native cache ahead of its persisted state. Read equality alone must therefore not acknowledge a Memory save or an already known wallet result.\n\nA failed Connect Four bot save also left the paused Flutter board without a scheduled retry. A completed move whose reward failed could similarly leave an unfinished result flow. Separately, the actual Android tour in run 43626348513 failed because general OCR fallbacks spent its existing preview-observation budget on a still fading frame.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Memory explicitly confirms validated native-cache snapshots using a positive same-value platform write acknowledgement at initial adoption and failure recovery. The existing owner queue, profile checks, save keys, rules and original 14 Dart-cache regression cases remain unchanged.\n- The three existing wallet result-ID deduplication paths require a positive persistence response before returning success. They do not add another reward or emit an extra wallet change.\n- Connect Four re-arms failed bot actions on the paused clock. A saved terminal move retries only its existing reward and receipt; its result display is delivered through the same paused clock with fresh owner/generation checks.\n- Only the exact Kart preview caption uses a fast whole-image OCR path. Two fresh observed frames, exact text and stable bounds, actual input and the original 55-second deadline remain required. All downstream race, HUD, driving, save and return gates remain unchanged.\n\n## Source and verification\n\nHead `e2db0d60af51266caa9b54ffd08eb0947ae99ac6`, parent `28462a7547048b75fa114e6f5832248e54c94faa`, complete tree `944a412a34a09ef24c3fb65c118e8a678809758f`.\n\nExactly nine file entries: six modifications and three added regression files. **4,363 earlier leaves remain byte-identical**, no deletions. Native remains `29080ef8cd1a5b385eeeec97976fbefd31280427`; version remains 0.13.8+2020.\n\n- **25 Python cases actually passed locally**, including two new cases and all 23 existing ones unchanged.\n- The actual new OCR reader was replayed against two unchanged PNGs from failed Android artifact 14127109230: the faded image remains negative; the clear image yields the complete actual caption and its observed bounds. This offline replay sends no touch and does not claim a new Android success.\n- **45 new Flutter cases are prepared**, separately reviewed: Memory 25, wallet 14, Connect Four 6. They have **not yet executed**. Existing CI is the required next gate; no local Dart/Flutter execution is claimed.\n- All nine source blobs were fully read back as UTF-8 and compared to exact local/Git hashes. Independent peer reviews and original negative evidence are retained.\n\nThis draft targets development Studio. Its branch is not yet promoted to Studio and no production Main ref is changed. API-level acknowledgement is not a physical fsync, multi-engine CAS, real Fold7 performance or APK release approval.\n\n## First actual CI attempt — failed before Flutter execution\n\n[Feature run 43632642356](https://github.com/Ullmann27/lumo-lernen/actions/runs/43632642356) failed in Flutter analysis and the Memory source compiler: `memory_round.dart:268:26` and `:277:26` cannot call the confirmation methods on the statically retained `MemoryStore` type. The 45 new cases and complete Flutter suite were not started. A two-line local-type correction is being prepared; this failed attempt and its original logs remain preserved.\n",
